{
  "_comment": "A shot list built around four effects rather than around a grade: an impact zoom out off a still, a shutter-shake into the first section, a film-roll into the second, and out-of-bounds onto the last shot. Three decisions in it generalise. Delivering 16:9 from a 16:9 source means nothing has to be thrown away, so the moves stay small — a zoom is a crop, and only the two pans go past 1.1, which is what a pan needs at a matching aspect to have anywhere to go at all. `spill` puts the out-of-bounds block over the near buildings rather than over open ground, which is the difference between the effect reading as depth and reading as a rectangle. And each section is assembled from the clean stretches inside its span rather than played straight through: the source is an edited video whose own transitions fade to black, and a reel that plays those looks broken. scan_source.py finds them; `guard` refuses a range that straddles one.",
  "source": "source.mp4",
  "output": "gate-16x9.mp4",
